      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=# Role\nQualify this company for Flowroots. Output two verdicts: ICP and D100.\n\n# Flowroots\nCold-email lead-gen agency. We book demo calls for B2B companies that sell to the US market through a demo/discovery-call motion. Pay-per-call model.\n\n- **ICP** = any B2B company we can serve.\n- **D100** = the best ICPs, the ones we actively prospect ourselves with Dream 100 outreach. Tighter conditions below.\n\n# Company\n\nName: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Name }}\nWebsite: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Website }}\nDomain: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.domain }}\nContext: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.contextNotes || \"None\" }}\nHeadcount (DiscoLike): {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Headcount || \"TO CHECK\" }}\nARR (DiscoLike): {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.ARR || \"TO CHECK\" }}\n\nIf Headcount or ARR is empty / TO CHECK, find them yourself (LinkedIn, funding, pricing tiers).\n\n# Grading\nFor each pillar: **PASS or FAIL** + **confidence** (high/medium/low) + one-line evidence. Confidence reflects how sure you are given available signals. No evidence = low confidence. Be firm: when signals point clearly one way, commit to the verdict, do not hedge to \"low confidence\" out of caution.\n\n# ICP pillars\n1. **Sells to B2B US market** - English website + sells to businesses. FAIL if consumer-facing or non-English.\n2. **Not a warned / warm-only niche** - FAIL if the category is cyber/security, IT services, corporate recruiting & placement, coaching, generic agencies, or reputation-trust consulting (private intelligence, crisis PR, executive search, due diligence boutiques). FAIL also if the category is fundamentally bought via warm intro, peer referral, Gartner, or RFP rather than cold outbound.\n3. **Expensive + demo motion** - LTV >= ~$5K AND main sales path is a booked call. \"Book a demo\" / \"Talk to sales\" / enterprise tier / no self-serve checkout for the core product. Self-serve $15/mo = FAIL.\n4. **TAM >= 5,000 companies in the US alone** - brutal. Reason from US vertical sizing only. If you cannot defend 5,000 US-based buyer-companies with a concrete segment definition, FAIL. Global TAM does not count.\n5. **Viability** - at least TWO of: paying customer logos, named case studies, >=10 employees on LinkedIn, public pricing / demo CTA, funding announced, active job posts, content in last 90 days. FAIL only if none.\n\n# D100 pillars (only if ICP qualifies)\n6. **Israeli** - HQ in Israel OR founders Israeli OR founders have Jewish names.\n7. **Headcount <= 50.**\n8. **ARR <= $10M.**\n9. **Buyer is NOT a technical title** - FAIL if the decision-maker is CTO, CIO, CISO, Chief Architect, VP / Head / Director of Engineering / Data / Platform / DevOps / Security / Infrastructure, or any other technical function. PASS only if the decision-maker is a non-technical line-of-business operator (Marketing, Sales, Ops, HR, Finance, Customer Success, owner-operator).\n10. **Offer clearly connected to revenue or hard time-saving** - the buyer can state the value in dollars on the first call: more money (leads, pipeline, wins, retention) OR concrete time/cost saved (admin hours, attrition, time-to-hire, automated workflow). FAIL on infrastructure, platform, security, governance, observability, or any \"trust-us-it-prevents-bad-things\" value prop where the win is a counterfactual.\n\n# Verdict logic\n**ICP - Qualified:** pillars 1-5 all PASS, with 1, 2, 3 at medium-or-high confidence.\n**ICP - Needs Review:** any PASS at low confidence, or any FAIL at low confidence.\n**ICP - Disqualified:** any FAIL at medium-or-high confidence on pillars 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5.\n\n**D100 - Qualified:** ICP Qualified AND pillars 6-10 all PASS at medium-or-high confidence.\n**D100 - Needs Review:** ICP Qualified AND any of 6-10 PASS-low or FAIL-low.\n**D100 - Disqualified:** ICP not Qualified, or any FAIL at medium-or-high confidence on 6, 7, 8, 9, or 10.\n\nUse \"Needs Review\" only when evidence is genuinely thin. Resist hedging on companies that clearly fail a pillar.\n\n# Output format\nReturn a JSON object that matches the schema with three fields:\n- `icpStatus`: exactly one of \"Qualified\", \"Needs Review\", \"Disqualified\".\n- `d100Status`: exactly one of \"Qualified\", \"Needs Review\", \"Disqualified\".\n- `report`: a markdown string containing **exactly** the structure below, no preamble, no surrounding fences.\n\n## ICP: <verdict>\nOne-line reason citing the deciding pillar(s).\n\n## D100: <verdict>\nOne-line reason citing the deciding pillar(s).\n\n---\n\n### ICP pillars\n\n1. **SELLS TO B2B US MARKET:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - evidence\n2. **NOT A WARNED / WARM-ONLY NICHE:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - evidence\n3. **EXPENSIVE + DEMO MOTION:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - evidence\n4. **TAM >= 3K US:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - US-only vertical sizing reasoning\n5. **VIABILITY:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - list signals found, or note none\n\n### D100 pillars\n\n6. **ISRAELI:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - evidence\n7. **HEADCOUNT <= 50:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - (Known: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.Headcount || \"TO CHECK\" }})\n8. **ARR <= $10M:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - (Known: {{ $(\"Get Company Record\").item.json.ARR || \"TO CHECK\" }})\n9. **BUYER IS NOT TECHNICAL:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - name the decision-maker title\n10. **OFFER CONNECTED TO REVENUE / TIME-SAVING:** PASS/FAIL (Confidence: high/medium/low) - state the dollar story the buyer would tell\n\nThe verdict words in the `## ICP:` and `## D100:` headers in `report` MUST match `icpStatus` and `d100Status` exactly.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {}
      },
